      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:08 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0000-0002",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "APPEARANCES:\nTOBY CROUSE, Solicitor General, Topeka, Kansas; on behalf of the Petitioner.\nMICHAEL R. HUSTON, Assistant to the Solicitor General, Department of Justice, Washington, D.C.; for the United States, as amicus curiae, supporting the Petitioner.\nSARAH E. HARRINGTON, ESQ., Bethesda, Maryland; on behalf of the Respondent."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Toby Crouse",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Reasonable suspicion is a minimal standard. It permits a brief investigation upon an officer's objective and particularized suspicion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Crouse, many of those cases that you referenced involved at least an officer who testified, speaking about, in his experience, drivers tend to be owners. We don't have anything like that here."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I admit there's three cases that hold that, but not 11. The others do talk extensively about the officer's experience."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Michael R. Huston for the United States",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Fourth Amendment asks police officers to be reasonable. It does not ask them to set aside common sense when they step into the patrol car."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: The -- you say it's reasonable to infer that the owner is the driver, but it's a little less reasonable, is it not, when the owner's license has been suspended?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But you just said, Mr. -- Mr. Huston, marginally less. How do you know that, that it's only marginally less as opposed to significantly less?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: I guess what I'm trying to say is, what is that common-sense judgment based on? I mean, I understand that if -- this goes back to Justice Gorsuch's question -- if it were based on a particular officer's training and experience and judgment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 30,
        "start": 30
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: But getting to the particular person, doesn't that have to do with geography? Meaning I suspect there are some towns in the United States where people don't break the law no matter what, that it would be -- you know, if your license got suspended, the police officer knows that in this jurisdiction, that presumption is not a good one."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0008",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: Excuse me. That is a generalized statistic then, though, that --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 32,
        "start": 32
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, let me give you a -- a hypothetical. Suppose that a municipality has a law that says everybody has to carry their driver's license with them at all times. And suppose that a particular police department actually did a kind of survey or, you know, a -- a -- a study of their practices and found that, actually, 50 percent of teenagers do not carry their driver's license with them at all times."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0010",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: So it's the same hypothetical as Justice Kagan's, but then distinguish that from this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Sarah E. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0012",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Kansas and the United States ask this Court to adopt a bright-line nationwide rule that it is always reasonable to assume that a car is being driven by its unlicensed owner. But, in three briefs and now 27 minutes of oral argument, they have offered literally no way for this Court to assess whether that is, in fact, a reasonable assumption, whether it is, in fact, based on common sense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Sarah E. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0013",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 37,
        "start": 37
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "to suspect that Mr. Glover was driving. But the officer stipulated that, actually, he had no idea who was driving. And the officer decided not to come in and testify at the suppression hearing to explain why he would assume that an unlicensed driver would be driving his car."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Sarah E. Harrington",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0001-0015",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "question isn't whether an owner usually drives his car but whether an owner who doesn't have a valid license usually --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 49,
        "start": 49
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: In your -- in your opening, you said it would be relatively easy for the police to establish whether the driver is the owner. What are you basing that on?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Well, if -- if it is and if your answer to Justice Ginsburg is correct that all an officer has to say is, in my training or experience, one out of 10, one out of 20, it's -- it's been the driver who is the owner of an unregistered car --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0003-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 73,
        "start": 73
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you think in Terry they needed statistics about the percentage of people who walked by a window three times who have some criminal intent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-556",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "efd3f60c6f52c0fd19b23e82a96d4b1c84d12dcbf04e379693f0f9a5f4bf0088",
      "evidence_id": "ev-efd3f60c6f52-0003-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 80,
        "start": 80
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: May I go back to the stipulation? You said it's -- Kansas drew the stipulation, right?"
    },
    {
